<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:16:30 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>France to send interceptor missiles to Ukraine after Russian strikes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260822-france-to-send-interceptor-missiles-to-ukraine-after-russian-strikes</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Saturday announced Paris would deliver new interceptor missiles to Ukraine, with Kyiv's air defences running short after the latest round of deadly Russian attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ba90ba6-9d7e-11f1-ad58-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T192414Z-1904355796-RC2H2NACS2W0-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ba90ba6-9d7e-11f1-ad58-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T192414Z-1904355796-RC2H2NACS2W0-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7339d4d2-9e2e-11f1-8d94-efa8280ce22b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:52:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ba90ba6-9d7e-11f1-ad58-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T192414Z-1904355796-RC2H2NACS2W0-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Oleksandr Ratushniak / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Still waters run deep: why Palme d'or winner 'Fjord' questions our certainties</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/culture/20260822-why-palme-d-or-winner-fjord-questions-our-certainties-cristian-mungiu-interview</link><description>
An isolated village in Norway sees its peaceful veneer upset by the arrival of a new family in Fjord, the Palme d'Or-winning film released in French cinemas this week. Inspired by real-life cases, Romanian director Cristian Mungiu explores questions of domestic violence, religion, culture and tolerance through a story that asks whose version of the truth can be trusted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d308978-5308-11f1-b3f1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/204424-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d308978-5308-11f1-b3f1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/204424-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a886d300-9bd2-11f1-be57-bfebf5b206b8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:05:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d308978-5308-11f1-b3f1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/204424-2.jpg">© Why Not Productions</source><dc:creator>Ollia Horton with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ravaged by wildfires, France's Fontainebleau forest reopens to public</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-france-s-fontainebleau-forest-reopens-to-public-after-wildfires</link><description>
The forest of Fontainebleau outside Paris has partially reopened to the public after remaining off-limits for over a month due to devastating wildfires. From Saturday, visitors can access some 80 percent of the forest, but are being warned to show caution around fragile wildlife and precarious trees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b21100-9e04-11f1-bb3d-976fc488f692</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg">© AFP - SIMON WOHLFAHRT </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Diplomats urge France and UK to uphold rule of law in Palestinian territories</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260822-former-envoys-urge-joint-french-uk-action-on-palestinian-territories</link><description>
Dozens of former senior French and UK diplomats on Saturday urged their governments to work together to uphold international law in the Palestinian territories, accusing Israel of seeking to "destroy" any prospect of a viable Palestinian state.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f01b776-9e0e-11f1-b29d-1df8a6684097</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:46:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg">© Ilia YEFIMOVICH / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Turkey, Saudi Arabia and Pakistan strengthen ties as Israel tensions rise</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260822-turkey-saudi-arabia-and-pakistan-strengthen-ties-as-israel-tensions-rise</link><description>
Tensions between Turkey and Israel have intensified after an Israeli airstrike targeted a Syrian military airbase near the Turkish border. The strike came days after Turkey’s new military pact with Saudi Arabia and Pakistan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d4b7ad0e-9255-11f1-9f2e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-07T111511Z-1176211354-RC2NTMA0W6QT-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-DEFENCE-AGREEMENT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d4b7ad0e-9255-11f1-9f2e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-07T111511Z-1176211354-RC2NTMA0W6QT-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-DEFENCE-AGREEMENT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39ae4a06-9d55-11f1-9576-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 08:07:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French farmers dip into winter fodder as drought leaves pastures bare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-french-farmers-dip-into-winter-fodder-as-drought-leaves-pastures-bare</link><description>
Repeated heatwaves and drought have made it a punishing summer for French farmers – scorching pastures, straining livestock and driving up costs. With grass disappearing from fields, cattle farmers across the country are already dipping into fodder meant to feed their herds through winter.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44161466-9d40-11f1-9260-c93d65df09a9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 07:04:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg">© Zeenat Hansrod</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>More Russians seeking to leave as fears of another mobilisation grow</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-mobilisation-fears-fuel-renewed-russian-interest-in-leaving-the-country-relokatz</link><description>
Fears of another military mobilisation are driving an increasing number of Russians to look at exiting the country, an emigration support platform has told RFI, nearly four years after Moscow called up 300,000 reservists to fight in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef236b40-bc0b-11f0-a79b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-83DB7ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef236b40-bc0b-11f0-a79b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-83DB7ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a977f20-9d41-11f1-817b-c93d65df09a9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:03:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef236b40-bc0b-11f0-a79b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-83DB7ZQ.jpg">© Andrej Isakovic / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>'An invisible avalanche': what happened in Cameroon's 1986 Lake Nyos disaster?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-an-invisible-avalanche-what-happened-in-cameroon-s-1986-lake-nyos-disaster</link><description>
On 21 August, 1986, 1,746 people died from carbon dioxide poisoning after gas escaped overnight from the bottom of Lake Nyos in Cameroon. RFI examines what happened in the world's deadliest "limnic eruption" and how, 40 years later, our understanding of the danger posed by volcanic lakes is still evolving. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6970f48a-1541-11ea-b2e0-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/lake_nyos_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6970f48a-1541-11ea-b2e0-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/lake_nyos_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f1af974-9d4c-11f1-8f6e-f35f06fd4b75</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:47:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6970f48a-1541-11ea-b2e0-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/lake_nyos_0.jpg">Wikipedia/Domaine public</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo Ebola outbreak 'growing exponentially' with more than 2,500 dead</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-dr-congo-ebola-outbreak-growing-exponentially-with-more-than-2-500-dead</link><description>
The Ebola outbreak raging in the Democratic Republic of Congo is growing "exponentially", with more than 2,500 deaths recorded and half of those in the last 20 days, the senior UN coordinator on the disease said Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">837f67ba-9d54-11f1-9288-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:36:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg">© Jospin Mwisha / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France backs down on plan to make patients pay more for healthcare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260821-france-backs-down-on-plan-to-make-patients-pay-more-for-healthcare-medicine</link><description>
The French government has scrapped plans to double the annual ceiling on out-of-pocket charges for medicines, medical appointments and other healthcare, after criticism from patient groups and health professionals. The cap was due to rise from €100 to €200, but the government will instead pursue a smaller increase linked to inflation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">264a2d16-9d52-11f1-8885-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:45:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg">AP - Daniel Cole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and European allies press Israel to abandon West Bank settlement plan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-france-and-european-allies-press-israel-to-abandon-west-bank-settlement-plan</link><description>
France has joined Germany, Italy and the United Kingdom in calling on Israel to halt the expansion of settlements illegal under international law in the occupied West Bank, and immediately withdraw tenders issued this week for more than 1,200 new homes under the controversial E1 project.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8e5c86c-9d29-11f1-b0f3-e1f7ae7eac67</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 07:01:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg">©  OHAD ZWIGENBERG / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Cameroon’s President Biya home after 73-day absence, amid health speculation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-cameroon-president-biya-home-after-73-day-absence-amid-health-speculation</link><description>
Cameroon’s President Paul Biya has returned to the country after spending 73 days abroad, ending an unusually long absence that has intensified speculation around the 93-year-old’s health and raised questions over Cameroon's political future.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff0dfbf0-9d34-11f1-a29e-831a4ab27004</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:11:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg">AP - Sunday Alamba</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>West Bank village siege fuels concern over growing settler violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-west-bank-village-siege-fuels-concern-over-growing-settler-violence-qusra</link><description>
Palestinian families remained trapped in their homes in the occupied West Bank village of Qusra for an 11th day on Thursday, in a case that has drawn condemnation from US Ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee and become a symbol of growing settler violence in the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f68c4d44-9ca1-11f1-918c-f35507a1bea8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:20:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg">AFP - ZAIN JAAFAR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Spain to open shelters in Ceuta for migrants and transfer 500 girls to mainland</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-spain-to-open-shelters-in-ceuta-for-migrants-and-transfer-500-girls-to-mainland</link><description>
Spain will open temporary shelters for up to 1,800 migrants in Ceuta, its enclave in Morocco, as authorities tackle the humanitarian crisis resulting from tens of thousands of people attempting to enter the territory last month. The government is also preparing to transfer 500 unaccompanied migrant girls to mainland Spain, despite opposition from Ceuta authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b17bfa10-9c83-11f1-8237-a5c3347b2fe8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:45:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Violeta Santos Moura/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French hospital helicopter landings disrupted by illegal prison delivery drones</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-french-hospital-helicopter-landings-disrupted-by-illegal-prison-delivery-drones</link><description>
Emergency helicopter landings at Strasbourg University Hospitals have been suspended over the risk of collision with drones used to illegally deliver items to inmates in a nearby prison. The hospital says the resulting detour could be "life-threatening" for patients.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cbfa0aba-9c99-11f1-89cd-cf462987716b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:09:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg">© Gabriel BOUYS / AFP/Archives</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rights group calls for release of two French journalists held in Togo</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-rights-group-calls-for-release-of-two-french-journalists-held-in-togo-ga%C3%ABl-moca%C3%ABr-sebastian-perez-pezzani</link><description>
Two French journalists detained in Togo since late July have been placed in pre-trial detention and charged with "false statements", Reporters Without Borders (RSF) has said, calling for their immediate release. 
